# User Rules for Response Formatting

- NEVER use LaTeX math mode (`$` or `$$`) in chat responses for variable names, formulas, or terms (e.g. do NOT write `$\text{FFM}_{\text{bruta}}$` or `$$\text{Masa Grasa} = ...$$`).
- Always write variable names, equations, and mathematical expressions using backticks (`...`) or clean plain text.
- Example: Write `Masa Grasa = Peso Total - FFM_bruta` instead of LaTeX math tags.
- NEVER run local web servers, browsers, or background rendering tools to test or preview the application. The user will always perform manual testing directly.

